      "content_fixes": [
        {
          "index": 17,
          "old": "When the king of Moab saw that he was losing, he took seven hundred swordsmen to try and break through the king of Edom's line, but they failed. Then he took his oldest son, the one who was supposed to be the next king, and sacrificed him on the city wall. This made God furious with Israel. So Israel pulled back and went home.",
          "new": "When the king of Moab saw that he was losing, he took seven hundred swordsmen to try and break through the king of Edom's line, but they failed. Then he took his oldest son, the one who was supposed to be the next king, and sacrificed him on the city wall. This set off furious anger against Israel. So Israel pulled back and went home.",
          "reason": "MSG 3:27 says \"set off furious anger against Israel\", not specifically God's anger; source over-identifies the anger as God's"
        }
      ],
